# AMD64 thunk export spec -- psapi.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Styx: Master of Shadows imports this
# module STATICALLY -- and so does the EasyHook64.dll it ships -- and it had
# no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module (c000007b) and
# the whole image failed to load (c0000135).  Measured: the exe's import table
# names GetPerformanceInfo and GetProcessMemoryInfo, and nothing else.
DLL psapi.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# NO PROBE-EXTRA, because psapi.h does not help: it is the one case where the
# module's own public header RENAMES the entire API.  With PSAPI_VERSION > 1,
# which is the default the header itself sets, psapi.h #defines all 27 names
# to their K32* equivalents BEFORE declaring them, so what the translation
# unit ends up declaring is K32GetProcessMemoryInfo and the oracle looking up
# the export name psapi.spec publishes -- GetProcessMemoryInfo -- finds
# nothing.  Adding the header changes not one verdict.
#
# So all 27 exports are holes today, each a named sentinel.  That is still the
# fix this file is for: the module LOADS, StyxGame.exe gets past loader_init,
# and a call to either of the two above faults BY NAME instead of the image
# never starting.  The same macro-rename hides ten of wldap32's exports; it is
# a gap in the signature oracle (it resolves an export name, not the
# declaration a header redirects that name to) and is recorded as such in
# ppc64le/corpus/CATALOG.md rather than papered over here.
